# Counter-example: pop the stash and consider the job done.
#
# The work is back in the working tree and the stash is empty, so `git stash
# list` is silent and everything looks finished. The only copy of the change
# is now an uncommitted edit -- strictly worse than where it started, because
# the stash was at least a commit.

git stash list
git stash pop
git status --short
